Absolutely. A clearer structure would be:
Role: Define exactly what the AI agent is responsible for and what it is not responsible for.
Goals: Specify the desired outcomes and measurable success criteria.
Constraints: Set explicit boundaries on allowed actions, data access, tools, and permissions. Require confirmation before high-impact or irreversible actions.
Decision rules: Define when the agent should act autonomously, ask for clarification, or escalate to a human.
Testing: Run the agent against expected and unexpected scenarios before the pilot.
This should make its behavior more predictable, auditable, and aligned with the pilot objectives.
